Orrin (to Ana): Ana. That's a good name for a river town. You'll want the eastern path, not the bridge — the bridge planks are rotten and the river's been high all week. And child... I've heard promises about lamp oil before. The sea keeps hers, the river keeps his, but people — people forget.
